 "text": "Hello, how are you holding up? Everyone can draw, it' just a matter of practice. Start with simple shapes and build up from there. Pick a blank page and start with simple shapes. Circles, squares and lines help you build up confidence. A rough drawing is quick and rough version of something, usually done in pen or pencil. A rough draft is a full size, detailed sketch. Rough drawing skills improve lot with practice. Lots of people never lose their childlike drawing skills.",
